<title>SWITZERLAND: WTO to rule on US-EC computer tariff dispute.</title>
<headline>WTO to rule on US-EC computer tariff dispute.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA</dateline>
<text>
<p>The World Trade Organisation has set up a panel to rule on a U.S. complaint against the European Community for its customs reclassification of certain computer equipment, a WTO spokesman said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The reclassification for tariff purpose covers certain Local Area Network (LAN) adapter equipment and personal computers with multimedia capability, which Washington alleges has resulted in higher duties being imposed on U.S. imports.</p>
<p>The U.S. trade delegation says the EC's reclassification of LAN adapter cards, begun in mid-1995, has affected hundreds of millions of dollars in U.S. exports.</p>
<p>EC tariffs on such products rose from the 3.5 percent imposed on automatic data processing machines to 7.5 percent imposed on telecommunications equipment, according to the U.S. complaint.</p>
</text>
